      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Economic sanctions are a highly controversial tool, and the reality is they are often a blunt instrument of foreign policy rather than a precise lever for democratic change. While proponents argue they force regimes to alter behavior, the overwhelming evidence shows they frequently cause immense suffering to the civilian population without achieving the desired political shift. Therefore, they are most accurately viewed as a form of economic coercion used by powerful nations to enforce their geopolitical will.",
      "source": "target",
